meta {
  name: Heartbeat
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attempts/{{attemptId}}/proctor-session/heartbeat
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  Proof of life, every ~15s in the browser. Its absence is the signal that matters:
  the easiest attack on a browser-side detector is to stop reporting, so the sweep
  task turns silence past `HEARTBEAT_GAP_SECONDS` into a `heartbeat_gap` event.
  A suspiciously clean session with a four-minute reporting hole is not a clean
  session — and the record says so without the client's help.
}
